{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>These are the generations, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory already darshened the verse (Genesis Rabbah, chapter 12), but its plain sense has not been made known." "<b>And it appears</b> that since the text had already informed us that HaShem said to the created beings that they too should produce generations — to the heavens, to divide the waters, and many other details as stated in their words; and to the earth He also said to bring forth living creatures and to bring forth fruit trees and grasses; and to the waters He said ״יִשְׁרְצוּ הַמַּיִם״ etc. — lest a person err and think that the earth and the heavens of their own accord performed the action, and this thought would produce defective generations, therefore the text comes and says <b>these are the generations of the heavens</b>, meaning: the generations that the heavens and the earth brought forth, matter of day by day, as written in the order of the days. Do not think that they made the things something from nothing, in the manner of the Creator, exalted be His name, who created everything something from nothing — not so; rather, ״בְּהִבָּרְאָם בְּיוֹם עֲשׂוֹת״, which is one day, on which HaShem created them with the power of creation that HaShem implanted in them — He created [it so] that they would bring forth what He had decreed upon them afterward, just as He created in man the power to beget, by way of the nature of creation that the Former, blessed be He, the Creator, imprinted in him, and man does nothing of himself; so too the heavens and the earth." "And the reason He mentioned only heavens and earth, and did not mention the waters, is that they are included in the heavens." "And the parsing of the word <b>behibbaram</b> is as though it said ״בָּהֶם בְּרָאָם״, meaning: for the generations mentioned. Or it may be parsed like the parsing of the word ״הֵילִיכִי״ (Exodus 2:9), and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah, chapter 1): this is שֶׁלִּיכִי; and likewise the text may intend by saying <b>behibbaram</b>, meaning: by means of those mentioned immediately above, He created them; and always, He who is the Former is He who is the Creator."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:29.925188685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}